      - (b) policyholders’ funds of Pension, Annuity business and Group business including funds of variable insurance products at their carrying value; 

      - (c) policyholders’ unit reserves of unit linked insurance business including funds of variable insurance products at their market value as per guidelines issued under these regulations, from time to time; 

   - (ii) in the case of General Insurer including an insurer carrying on business of reinsurance or health insurance or in case of a branch of a foreign company engaged in the business of re-insurance, funds maintained in its head office account, shareholders’ funds representing solvency margin and policyholders’ funds at their carrying value as shown in its balance sheet prepared in accordance with these regulations; 

