## **6. Unit Linked Insurance Business** 

- (1) Without prejudice to Sections 10 (2AA), 27 or 27A of the Act and any provisions of these regulations every insurer shall invest and at all times keep invested its segregated fund(s) under clause 3(3) (with underlying securities at custodian level) of Unit linked business as per pattern of investment offered to and subscribed to by the policy-holders where the units are linked to categories of assets which are both marketable and readily realizable within the approved pattern as per the product regulations. 

